  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Assistance to Vulnerable Populations in Northwest Syria (NWS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Of the eight sub-districts in Syria considered to be in extreme or catastrophic need, seven are located in northwest Syria (NWS). In NWS, there are 2.7 million internally displaced persons (IDPs), of which over one million are residing in last resort sites, in dire living situations. The ongoing COVID-19 pandemic continues to exacerbate humanitarian needs. Concurrently, the Syrian economy deteriorated greatly over the last year, including in NWS. This has exacerbated existing humanitarian vulnerabilities and increased the use of negative coping mechanisms. As a result, food insecurity has increased dramatically in NWS.</narrative>
  </description>
